// What a conversation's parts are called, for everything that writes or reads
// the session record (session.coax): the kind of a tool call (TK_*) and the
// kind of a notice (N_*). Plain numbers only: no text, no colours, no
// drawing. The engines (../engine/) write them; the chat components
// (components/zeron/tools.coax and transcript.coax load this file) show them.
// The numbers are kept in saved sessions and in the web chat's stream, so a
// new kind takes the next number and none is ever reused.

TK_THOUGHT :: 0; TK_EXEC :: 1; TK_READ :: 2; TK_EDIT :: 3; TK_SEARCH :: 4; TK_FETCH :: 5;
// The rest of Zeron's ToolCall kinds (proto view.rs tool_chip_content):
// Write, Glob, Web (a web search), Todo, MCP ("server · tool"), Agent (a
// subagent, its description) and any other tool by its name.
TK_WRITE :: 6; TK_GLOB :: 7; TK_WEB :: 8; TK_TODO :: 9; TK_MCP :: 10; TK_AGENT :: 11; TK_TOOL :: 12;
// The Lab's routing decision (lab.coax): who decided, in how long, and every distribution.
TK_ROUTE :: 13;
// A model loading on the GPU before its message goes (gpu.coax): the switch's answers.
TK_LOAD :: 14;

// A notice row: Zeron's ErrorChip (notice.rs notice_chip_with_action, the
// transcript's tile) for a failed turn, labelled as run_errors.rs reads the
// message ("Logged out" and "Limit reached" carry "Log in"); the same chip
// in Zeron's warning palette asking to approve a tool call (Allow, Deny);
// Claude Code missing (Install); and a quiet "Stopped" line under a turn
// the user stopped.
N_ERROR :: 0; N_SIGNED_OUT :: 1; N_LIMIT :: 2; N_INSTALL :: 3; N_STOPPED :: 4; N_ASK :: 5;
// Psionic's (psionic.coax): its one worker is busy; its server can't be reached.
N_BUSY :: 6; N_OFFLINE :: 7;
// openagents.com/chat's line under an answer: who wrote it, on whose key, what it cost (quiet, no tile).
N_META :: 8;
// Codex missing (codex.coax): Install, as for Claude Code.
N_CODEX_INSTALL :: 9;
